  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use existing Spring XD codebase and build system (Maven/Gradle).",
    "For DEBS challenge, assume remaining work is implementation of specific operators or sinks.",
    "CI build: add install target to existing CI pipeline (e.g., Maven install goal or custom script).",
    "Samples repo: publish as a GitHub repository or internal artifact repository with proper documentation.",
    "Performance benchmarks: use existing benchmark harness (e.g., JMH) and focus on jdbchdfs module.",
    "TupleBuilder benchmarking: use JMH for microbenchmarks, profile with async-profiler or similar.",
    "GPDB parameter UX: introduce a new parameter parser that handles escaping automatically, backward compatible.",
    "Migration to SPI: define a RuntimeSPI interface with methods for module deployment, lifecycle; refactor DeploymentManager to use SPI.",
    "ModuleRunner: create a Spring Boot application that uses Spring's classloader isolation (e.g., Spring Boot's Launcher) to run modules in isolation without xd-containers."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Developer has full access to the codebase and necessary environments (CI, benchmark, databases).",
    "The DEBS challenge deadline is fixed, but effort only covers development, not waiting for deadline.",
    "CI system is Jenkins or GitHub Actions; adding install target is straightforward.",
    "Samples repo is a GitHub organization; publishing means pushing a new repo or adding to existing.",
    "Benchmark environment (hardware, data) is available and configured.",
    "TupleBuilder is a standalone class; performance tuning does not require major architectural changes.",
    "GPDB and SQLServer instances are available for testing Sqoop jobs.",
    "The repository abstraction is limited to the deployment module; migration does not affect other modules heavily.",
    "ModuleRunner will be built on Spring Boot 2.x/3.x and Java 17+ (as per Spring Framework 6.0).",
    "All testing is done by the developer; no separate QA effort."
